# Purchasing through the gateway, in the order a reader would try it. Start the stack with `docker compose up`,
# then take a requisition through approval so Purchasing has a draft to work with.

@gateway = http://localhost:5300/api

### Bruno, a buyer: amends, issues and closes orders.
# @name bruno
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/matchbook/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=bruno&password=matchbook

### Rosa, a receiver: records what arrives. She may never be the buyer who issued the order.
# @name rosa
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/matchbook/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=rosa&password=matchbook

### Drafts waiting for a buyer, newest first; pass the page's next as ?after= for the following page.
# @name drafts
GET {{gateway}}/purchase-orders?status=Draft&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

@orderId = {{drafts.response.body.$.items[0].id}}

### One order, with ordered, received and invoiced quantities on every line.
# @name order
GET {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

### The same order found from its requisition, as a requisition screen would; 404 until the approval is processed.
GET {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/by-requisition/{{order.response.body.$.requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

### Change a draft line's quantity and price; zero keeps the line on the order, below zero is a 422.
PUT {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/lines/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 8, "unitPrice": 12.5 }

### Issue it: 202 and CommitmentPending until Budgets commits the funds, then Issued (read the order again).
POST {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/issue
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

### Rosa records a delivery under an id she chose, so a retry after a timeout cannot receive twice.
# @name receipt
POST {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{rosa.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "{{$guid}}", "lines": [ { "lineNumber": 1, "quantity": 5 } ] }

### The same receipt again: the first answer comes back and nothing more is received.
POST {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{rosa.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "{{receipt.response.body.$.id}}", "lines": [ { "lineNumber": 1, "quantity": 5 } ] }

### Every receipt against the order, oldest first.
GET {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{rosa.response.body.access_token}}

### One receipt, where the receipt's Location header points.
GET {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/receipts/{{receipt.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rosa.response.body.access_token}}

### Bruno trying to receive is a 403: only a receiver records receipts.
POST {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lines": [ { "lineNumber": 1, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### Short-close: nothing more will be received, Budgets releases what it still holds, invoices still count.
POST {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/short-close
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

### Cancel works on a draft, an order waiting for Budgets, or an issued order with nothing received; this one is a 409.
POST {{gateway}}/purchase-orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}

### Short-closed orders; every status filters the same way.
GET {{gateway}}/purchase-orders?status=ShortClosed
Authorization: Bearer {{bruno.response.body.access_token}}
